quran[9]{c,v,t}:
  6,36,"Only those who listen (sincerely) will respond (to you). As for the dead, Allah will resurrect them, and to Him, they shall be returned."
  6,37,"They say: ‘Why has a (visible) sign not been sent down to him from his Lord?’ Say: ‘Allah is indeed capable of sending down a sign, but most of them do not know (the secrets behind His actions).’"
  6,38,"There is no walking (or crawling) creature on the earth, nor a bird that flies with its wings, but they are species like yourselves (in several traits). We have not omitted anything in the Book. Then, they will be gathered to their Lord (in the end)."
  6,39,And those who reject Our revelations are deaf and dumb (and are trapped) in (manifold) darkness. And Allah leaves whomever He wills to stray and guides whomever He pleases to the straight path.
  6,40,"Say (to them): ‘What do you think: If Allah’s punishment comes upon you, or the Hour overtakes you, will you supplicate somebody other than Allah, if you are truthful?’"
  6,41,"Instead, it is only Him you will supplicate, and if He wills, He will remove (the affliction) that had caused you to supplicate Him, and you will forget whatever partners you ascribe to Him."
  6,42,"We had indeed sent (messengers) to (different) nations before you, then We afflicted them with hardships and sufferings so that they might humble themselves (to Us)."
  6,43,"So why did they not humble themselves when our punishment overtook them? Instead, their hearts had hardened, and Satan made what they used to do alluring to them."
  6,44,"So when they forgot what they had been reminded of, We opened the gates of all (good) things for them (to flourish abundantly), until, when they rejoiced in what they were given, We seized them suddenly (with terrible punishment), and they were struck with utter despair."
